# research.cronon (seeds-14 §2 macro) — the Labo notebook's chunks in cronon order. A chunk is a note-family
# entry on the research bench; this is the cronon projection of that bench's chunks (superseded retained).
# Coarser than the Set primitives, so it is a MACRO — never a kernel handler. Forward to the bench op.
# Invoke: macro.run name=research.cronon bench=<labo> —  (not , which macro.run reserves).
#
#!params bench,limit=500
research.note.timeline name="$bench" order=cronon limit="$limit"
